WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
You put one thousand pounds
into a savings account.

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:08.520
It pays five per cent compound
interest, added at the end of each year.

3
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:13.750
A friend says: five per cent times
twenty years is one hundred per cent.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.300
So it doubles in twenty years.

5
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.780
Is your friend right?

6
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.430
When does your money first
reach two thousand pounds?

7
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.420
In this mission, you'll see how compound
interest differs from simple interest.

8
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:29.460
Simple interest is the same every year.

9
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.990
Compound interest is added to the balance,

10
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.650
so next year's interest is
bigger: interest earns interest.

11
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.540
And you'll use the yearly
multiplier: at five per cent,

12
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.400
multiply by one point zero five.

13
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.920
Your mission: find when your
money has first doubled.
